query image (second crop) clearly displays a dark hole and a bright streak in this region. The reference images (crops 3, 4, 5) show similar textured structures but do not exhibit this specific combination of a dark hole and a bright streak in the same location. The first crop (ref0) is partially visible but does not show the hole. This suggests the features are unique to the query and likely anomalous. I will now finalize the decision.", "mode": "anomaly_detection", "anomaly_score": 0.85, "visual_evidence": ["Side-by-side comparison confirms the dark hole and bright streak are present in the query image but absent in the reference images within the same region.", "The reference images show natural variation in shape and texture, but none contain the specific defect-like features seen in the query."], "refutation_target": 0, "refutation_verdict": "not_found", "feature_status_update": "Both candidate features (dark_hole, bright_streak) were not found in the reference images within the compared region.", "remaining_candidate_features": ["dark_hole", "bright_streak"], "updated_score": 0.85, "action": "final", "confidence": 85, "args": "None"}], "error": null}, {"item_id": "D10_0020", "domain_code": "D10", "label_gt": 0, "mode": "anomaly_detection", "anomaly_score": 0.88, "rationale": "The side-by-side comparison confirms that the thin, vertical hook-like protrusion is unique to the query image. The reference images display natural shape variations (e.g., holes, crescents, elongated forms) but none exhibit this specific protrusion. Since the feature is not found in the reference pool, it is classified as an anomaly.", "n_turns": 2, "tools_used": ["tool_side_by_side"], "confidence": 92, "initial_score": 0.85, "candidate_features": [{"name": "Thin vertical hook protrusion", "location_hint": "Top center of the object", "looks_defect_like": true}], "remaining_features": [{"location_hint": "Top center", "looks_defect_like": true, "name": "Thin vertical hook protrusion"}], "refutation_verdicts": [{"turn": 2, "verdict": "not_found", "status": null}], "updated_score": 0.88, "history": [{"turn": 1, "thought": "The query image shows a textured object with a distinct, thin, hook-like protrusion extending upwards from the main body. I need to compare this shape against the reference images to see if this protrusion is a normal variation or an anomaly. The references show similar textured blobs but with different overall shapes (one has a hole, one is elongated, one is crescent-like). None of the references appear to have this specific thin, vertical hook shape. This makes the protrusion a strong candidate for an anomaly. I will initiate the refutation protocol by listing this feature and checking if it exists in the references.", "mode": "anomaly_detection", "anomaly_score": 0.85, "visual_evidence": ["Query image contains a thin, vertical, hook-like protrusion at the top center of the object.", "Reference images show objects with holes, crescent shapes, or elongated forms, but none exhibit this specific thin hook protrusion."], "refutation_target": 0, "remaining_candidate_features": [{"name": "Thin vertical hook protrusion", "location_hint": "Top center of the object", "looks_defect_like": true}], "action": "call_tool", "tool": "tool_side_by_side", "confidence": 75, "args": "{'bbox': [100, 100, 200, 200]}", "obs_keys": ["bbox", "n_crops", "composite_b64", "error", "interpretation"], "obs_error": null}, {"turn": 2, "action": "final", "anomaly_score": 0.88, "mode": "anomaly_detection", "refutation_target": 0, "refutation_verdict": "not_found", "remaining_candidate_features": [{"location_hint": "Top center", "looks_defect_like": true, "name": "Thin vertical hook protrusion"}], "thought": "The side-by-side crop confirms the protrusion is present in the query but absent in all four reference images. The references show other shape variations, but none match this specific hook. The feature survives refutation, confirming the anomaly.", "updated_score": 0.88, "confidence": 92, "visual_evidence": ["Side-by-side view shows the hook protrusion in the query column only.", "Reference columns show different shapes (hole, crescent, etc.) but no hook."]}], "error": null}, {"item_id": "D10_0024", "domain_code": "D10", "label_gt": 0, "mode": "anomaly_detection", "anomaly_score": 0.15, "rationale": "The suspected anomaly (the protrusion) is present in the normal reference images (specifically Ref 0), proving it is a natural variation of the object's shape rather than a defect.", "n_turns": 2, "tools_used": ["tool_side_by_side"], "confidence": 90, "initial_score": 0.75, "candidate_features": [{"name": "Elongated protrusion", "location_hint": "Top center of the main body", "looks_defect_like": true}], "remaining_features": [], "refutation_verdicts": [{"turn": 2, "verdict": "found_in_ref", "status": "The protrusion is a normal variation, confirmed by Reference 0."}], "updated_score": 0.15, "history": [{"turn": 1, "thought": "The query image shows a point cloud with a distinct, elongated protrusion extending upwards from the main body. Comparing this to the reference images, which show more compact, blob-like or slightly irregular shapes without such a sharp, thin extension, this protrusion appears to be a potential anomaly. I need to verify if this shape is a normal variation or a defect by checking the references more closely.", "mode": "anomaly_detection", "anomaly_score": 0.75, "visual_evidence": ["Query image has a prominent, thin, upward-pointing protrusion.", "Reference images show compact, rounded, or slightly irregular blobs without such sharp extensions."], "refutation_target": 0, "remaining_candidate_features": [{"name": "Elongated protrusion", "location_hint": "Top center of the main body", "looks_defect_like": true}], "action": "call_tool", "tool": "tool_side_by_side", "confidence": 70, "args": "{'bbox': [80, 40, 180, 200]}", "obs_keys": ["bbox", "n_crops", "composite_b64", "error", "interpretation"], "obs_error": null}, {"turn": 2, "thought": "The side-by-side comparison reveals that the 'protrusion' I identified in the query is actually a common feature. Reference image 0 (second from left) shows a very similar, if not identical, upward-pointing protrusion. Reference image 2 also shows a smaller, detached piece that could be a variation of this feature. Since the feature exists in the normal reference pool, it is not an anomaly. The initial hypothesis is refuted.", "mode": "anomaly_detection", "anomaly_score": 0.15, "visual_evidence": ["The side-by-side view shows that Reference 0 has a similar upward protrusion.", "Reference 2 also shows a detached fragment, indicating shape variation is normal."], "refutation_verdict": "found_in_ref", "feature_status_update": "The protrusion is a normal variation, confirmed by Reference 0.", "remaining_candidate_features": [], "updated_score": 0.15, "action": "final", "confidence": 90}], "error": null}, {"item_id": "D10_0036", "domain_code": "D10", "label_gt": 0, "mode": "anomaly_detection", "anomaly_score": 0.92, "rationale": "The side-by-side comparison confirms the query object is structurally anomalous. While the reference images show large, coherent, textured shapes, the query image contains only tiny, fragmented specks. This feature (extreme fragmentation and small size) is not found in any of the reference images, confirming it as a defect.", "n_turns": 2, "tools_used": ["tool_side_by_side"], "confidence": 95, "initial_score": 0.85, "candidate_features": [{"name": "Size and Fragmentation", "location_hint": "center-bottom", "looks_defect_like": "The object is extremely small and appears as a few disconnected specks, unlike the solid, larger shapes in the references."}], "remaining_features": [{"looks_defect_like": "The object is extremely small and appears as a few disconnected specks, unlike the solid, larger shapes in the references.", "location_hint": "center-bottom", "name": "Size and Fragmentation"}], "refutation_verdicts": 